WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
NWSAPI v3: a clearer path to your next change.
1. Set up. 2. Find and edit. 3. Review.

00:06.000 --> 00:10.000
In a terminal, open the repository folder.
Type pnpm run setup, then press Enter.

00:10.000 --> 00:14.000
Setup installs tools, dependencies, and build outputs.
Wait for “Setup complete” before moving on.

00:14.000 --> 00:18.500
Type pnpm run guide, then press Enter.
This opens the documentation in your browser.

00:18.500 --> 00:23.000
Choose a document from the page-title menu.
Search all documents, or filter by topic and type.

00:23.000 --> 00:27.500
Find the section relevant to your task.
Then edit your source or documentation.

00:27.500 --> 00:32.000
Return to a saved section later.
Reading mode reduces visual motion.

00:32.000 --> 00:36.500
After editing, type pnpm run review and press Enter.
It runs lint, formatting, types, and unit tests in order.

00:36.500 --> 00:41.000
Fix the first reported issue and rerun.
Finish with git diff to inspect your changes.

00:41.000 --> 00:44.500
Missing tool or wrong version?
Type pnpm run setup:check, then press Enter.

00:44.500 --> 00:48.000
It checks Node.js, package managers, and checkout tools.
It reports readiness without changing your tools.
